<title>UK: Hays buys Germany's Daufenbach.</title>
<headline>Hays buys Germany's Daufenbach.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>British distribution and services company Hays Plc said on Thursday it bought Daufenbach GmbH, a German automotive components distributor, for an initial cash payment of 55 million marks.</p>
<p>THe company said it would also adopt existing borrowings of around 13 million marks and cash payments of up to nine million marks may become payable depending on Daufenbach's profit in the period from completion to December 31, 1997.</p>
<p>Hays said Daufenbach's operating profit totalled 7.5 million marks in the first 10 months of 1996.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
